H('461.d.1.B',3,"A clinic charts a patient's temperature over three days. The chart helps staff see whether the fever is:","going up or down",["a rumor","a prize","a contract"],"Graphs show trends in data.")
H('461.d.1.B',4,"A graph shows a child's weight at each visit. A line that rises steadily suggests the child is:","gaining weight over time",["losing weight","staying exactly the same","moving away"],"Trends appear in graphs.")
H('461.d.1.C',3,"A technician reads a manual explaining how to clean an ultrasound probe. Understanding this kind of text is called interpreting:","technical material",["fiction","poetry","advertising"],"Manuals give precise steps.")
H('461.d.1.C',4,"A nurse reads a package insert that lists side effects and storage rules. The insert is useful because it gives:","accurate product information",["entertainment","opinions","slogans"],"Inserts guide safe use.")
H('461.d.1.D',3,"At the end of a shift, a nurse summarizes a patient's changes in a clear note. This is an example of writing:","a report or summary",["a novel","a poem","a joke"],"Clear writing supports care.")
H('461.d.1.D',4,"A good patient summary is accurate, brief, and organized so the next shift can quickly find the:","key facts",["office gossip","lunch menu","parking rules"],"Summaries must be useful.")
H('461.d.1.E',3,"A student will explain hand hygiene to classmates. Planning an effective talk includes knowing the audience and rehearsing the:","main points",["jokes only","tiny details","wrong order"],"Preparation improves delivery.")
H('461.d.1.E',4,"To keep an oral presentation on health topics clear, a speaker should use an introduction, key points, and a:","conclusion",["secret","quiz grade","price list"],"Good talks have a structure.")
H('461.d.1.F',3,"A nurse says the patient has high blood pressure instead of saying her pressure is up there somewhere. The nurse is using:","precise language",["vague language","slang only","silence"],"Precision avoids errors.")
H('461.d.1.F',4,"Telling a patient exactly when to take a medicine and with what, rather than saying later, is an example of:","clear communication",["avoidance","delay","guessing"],"Clear instructions protect patients.")
H('461.d.1.G',3,"The body keeps its temperature steady by sweating when hot and shivering when cold. This balance is called:","homeostasis",["inflation","erosion","evolution"],"Homeostasis keeps stable conditions.")
H('461.d.1.G',4,"When blood sugar rises after a meal, the pancreas releases insulin to bring it back down. This is a chemical process that helps maintain:","balance in the body",["a school schedule","a bank account","a fashion trend"],"Hormones regulate balance.")
H('461.d.1.H',3,"A caregiver bends at the knees and keeps the patient close when lifting. Using good body mechanics protects the caregiver's:","back",["hair","phone","car"],"Proper mechanics prevent injury.")
H('461.d.1.H',4,"A wide base of support helps a person stay balanced when moving a patient because it lowers the chance of:","falling",["laughing","reading","sleeping"],"Balance depends on base of support.")
H('461.d.1.I',3,"In Maslow's hierarchy, needs like food, water, and sleep are at the bottom and are called:","physiological needs",["esteem needs","self-actualization","belonging"],"Basic survival needs come first.")
H('461.d.1.I',4,"A patient who feels safe, loved, and respected is meeting needs higher in the hierarchy than food and rest, such as:","belonging and esteem",["oxygen","water","shelter only"],"Higher needs follow basic needs.")
H('461.d.1.J',3,"Human development from birth to old age is divided into stages. The stage between childhood and adulthood is:","adolescence",["infancy","toddlerhood","late adulthood"],"Teen years are adolescence.")
H('461.d.1.J',4,"A health worker who works with older adults should understand the changes of late adulthood, such as slower:","reaction time",["growth spurts","tooth eruption","first steps"],"Aging changes needs.")
H('461.d.1.K',3,"Eating balanced meals, exercising, and sleeping enough are habits that support lifelong:","health and wellness",["debt","fame","boredom"],"Healthy habits help at every age.")
H('461.d.1.K',4,"Wellness means more than the absence of illness. It includes physical, mental, and social:","well-being",["rumors","costs","errors"],"Wellness is broad.")
H('461.d.1.L',3,"A health worker greets a patient warmly, listens, and explains things simply. These skills help build a healthy:","relationship with the patient",["bank balance","parking space","budget"],"Good communication builds trust.")
H('461.d.1.L',4,"Active listening and an open attitude help a care team keep relationships healthy because patients feel:","respected and heard",["ignored","rushed","judged"],"Respect improves cooperation.")
H('461.d.1.M',3,"In the past, doctors sometimes treated illness by draining blood. Studying how medicine has changed over time is learning the:","history of health care",["map of a city","rules of a sport","recipe for bread"],"History shows progress.")
H('461.d.1.M',4,"The discovery of germs in the 1800s led to cleaner hospitals and fewer infections. This is a key moment in the history of:","health care",["fashion","music","farming only"],"Germ theory changed medicine.")
H('461.d.1.N',3,"Hospitals, clinics, and pharmacies employ millions of people and spend billions each year. Health services therefore have a large effect on the:","economy",["weather","calendar","moon"],"Health care is a major industry.")
H('461.d.1.N',4,"When a community has a new hospital, jobs and local business often increase. This shows health services can help a community's:","economic growth",["school colors","weather","street names"],"Hospitals bring jobs.")
H('461.d.1.O',3,"Laws about patient privacy, medicine safety, and insurance are made by local, state, and national:","government",["sports leagues","fan clubs","game shows"],"Governments regulate health care.")
H('461.d.1.O',4,"Medicare and Medicaid are national programs that help pay for care. They are examples of government's effect on:","health care access",["road repair","sports rules","fashion"],"Government programs shape access.")
H('461.d.1.P',3,"A hospital offers translators and respects different religious customs. This shows how diverse cultures influence modern:","health care",["traffic","architecture only","weather"],"Culture shapes care.")
H('461.d.1.P',4,"Many medicines today began as plant remedies used by early cultures. This shows how cultural traditions have influenced:","modern medicine",["movie plots","sports uniforms","road signs"],"Traditional knowledge influenced drugs.")
H('461.d.1.Q',3,"Acupuncture developed in China, and herbal healing is practiced in many societies. Comparing these shows that cultures use different:","approaches to healing",["languages for math","kinds of weather","school buses"],"Cultures treat illness differently.")
H('461.d.1.Q',4,"A health worker who learns about a patient's cultural health beliefs can offer care that is:","respectful and effective",["rushed","secret","expensive"],"Understanding culture improves care.")
H('461.d.2.A',3,"Making eye contact, speaking clearly, and listening are parts of effective communication. Interrupting and mumbling are parts of:","non-effective communication",["teamwork","good listening","active speaking"],"Behaviors shape communication.")
H('461.d.2.A',4,"A message gets lost when a nurse uses medical words that the patient does not know. This is a barrier to:","understanding",["breathing","walking","hearing aids"],"Jargon blocks understanding.")
H('461.d.2.B',3,"A patient is anxious about surgery. The best communication response is to speak calmly and:","listen to the concerns",["change the subject","tell them to stop worrying","leave the room"],"Empathy helps anxious patients.")
H('461.d.2.B',4,"A patient who speaks little English needs care. A health worker should arrange for a qualified:","interpreter",["decorator","driver","cook"],"Interpreters bridge language gaps.")
H('461.d.2.C',3,"Two coworkers disagree about a schedule. A good conflict-resolution technique is to listen to both and look for a:","compromise",["winner","punishment","rumor"],"Compromise settles conflicts.")
H('461.d.2.C',4,"Techniques such as staying calm, using I statements, and focusing on the problem work best when the goal is to:","solve the conflict",["win the argument","embarrass a coworker","avoid talking"],"Resolution is the aim.")
H('461.d.2.D',3,"Knowing that the prefix hyper means above normal, a nurse understands that hypertension means blood pressure that is:","too high",["too low","normal","absent"],"Word parts reveal meaning.")
H('461.d.2.D',4,"In carditis, the root cardi names the organ that pumps blood and itis means inflammation, so carditis is inflammation of the:","heart",["lungs","liver","stomach"],"Medical terms combine word parts.")
H('461.d.3.A',3,"A person who motivates others, stays honest, and makes fair decisions shows the traits of a good:","leader",["critic","bystander","rival"],"Leaders model good traits.")
H('461.d.3.A',4,"Responsibility, integrity, and the ability to inspire a team are examples of:","leadership traits",["fixed salaries","exam questions","hospital rooms"],"Traits make leaders effective.")
H('461.d.3.B',3,"A student officer in HOSA organizes a service project and thanks volunteers. This demonstrates:","leadership skills",["avoidance","absence","confusion"],"Leaders organize and recognize others.")
H('461.d.3.B',4,"A team leader who takes responsibility for a mistake and helps fix it shows:","accountability",["blame","rumors","delay"],"Leaders own their results.")
H('461.d.3.C',3,"At a meeting, the chair uses an agenda and gives everyone a chance to speak. This helps the group to:","stay organized and fair",["run out of time","avoid decisions","create conflict"],"Agendas focus meetings.")
H('461.d.3.C',4,"Taking minutes during a meeting creates a record of what was decided and who will:","do each task",["win the debate","pay for lunch","order supplies"],"Minutes record actions.")
H('461.d.4.A',3,"A student uses a state labor website to compare the pay and training needed for several health careers. This is researching:","career options",["sports scores","movie times","recipes"],"Reliable sources show career data.")
H('461.d.4.A',4,"To judge whether an employment website is reliable, a student should check who runs it and whether the data are:","current and sourced",["colorful","loud","long"],"Credible sources matter.")
H('461.d.4.B',3,"Choosing to leave school early can limit a person's later job options. This shows a career decision can have long-term:","effects",["rains","sounds","colors"],"Choices have consequences.")
H('461.d.4.B',4,"A student weighs the cost of training against the pay of a career. This is thinking about the causes and effects of a:","career decision",["weather forecast","school bus route","sports game"],"Planning compares costs and benefits.")
H('461.d.6.A',3,"An X-ray technologist helps find disease, while a physical therapist helps people recover movement. These careers are in the diagnostic and:","therapeutic areas",["farming areas","culinary areas","retail areas"],"Careers are grouped by function.")
H('461.d.6.A',4,"A medical laboratory technician tests blood samples, while a nurse delivers daily care. The lab technician works in the diagnostic area, and the nurse works mostly in the:","therapeutic area",["research office","sales department","accounting office"],"Different pathways serve different roles.")
H('461.d.6.B',3,"A patient with a broken leg may see an emergency physician, a radiology technologist, and a physical therapist. These team members work together to deliver:","complete care",["confusing care","unrelated care","slow care"],"Care depends on teamwork.")
H('461.d.6.B',4,"The respiratory therapist tells the nurse that the patient needs more oxygen. This sharing of information between team members improves:","patient care",["parking","scheduling only","billing only"],"Collaboration improves outcomes.")
H('461.d.7.A',3,"A doctor, a nurse, a pharmacist, and a dietitian work together to plan a patient's care. This is the concept of:","teaming",["competing","isolating","avoiding"],"Teams provide quality care.")
H('461.d.7.A',4,"When team members respect each other's roles and share information, the patients receive:","safer, better care",["slower care","confusing care","less care"],"Teaming improves quality.")
H('461.d.7.B',3,"HOSA-Future Health Professionals and the American Nurses Association are examples of:","professional organizations",["sports teams","film studios","grocery stores"],"These groups support training and standards.")
H('461.d.7.B',4,"A professional organization helps its members by offering continuing education and setting standards for their:","work",["vacations","hairstyles","hobbies"],"Associations support the profession.")
H('461.d.8.A',3,"A code of ethics lists the duties of a profession, while a scope of practice describes what a worker is legally allowed to:","do",["wear","eat","own"],"Scope sets legal limits.")
H('461.d.8.A',4,"A certified nursing assistant is asked to give a medicine only a nurse may give. Staying within the scope of practice, she should:","decline and tell the nurse",["do it quietly","guess the dose","ask a patient"],"Workers follow their scope.")
H('461.d.8.B',3,"A health worker who tells a stranger about a patient's illness has broken:","confidentiality",["a schedule","a vacation","a dress code"],"Privacy must be protected.")
H('461.d.8.B',4,"HIPAA is a law that protects the privacy of a patient's:","health information",["car insurance","school grades","bus pass"],"HIPAA protects medical data.")
H('461.d.8.C',3,"Questions about who gets a limited organ for transplant, or whether to continue treatment, are called ethical issues in:","health care",["sports","cooking","fashion"],"Hard choices arise in medicine.")
H('461.d.8.C',4,"A patient with a serious illness decides to refuse treatment. Ethically, a competent patient has the right to:","make decisions about care",["be ignored","be forced to accept care","lose all privacy"],"Autonomy is a core principle.")
H('461.d.8.D',3,"When a health worker fails to give care that a reasonable worker would give and the patient is harmed, it may be called:","negligence",["kindness","teamwork","fundraising"],"Negligence is failure to meet the standard of care.")
H('461.d.8.D',4,"A legal responsibility for harm caused by a mistake in care is called:","liability",["luck","charity","punctuality"],"Liability carries legal risk.")
H('461.d.8.E',3,"Health workers must follow state and federal laws, such as those about reporting suspected abuse and protecting:","patient records",["lunch menus","uniform colors","parking rules"],"Laws guide practice.")
H('461.d.8.E',4,"Licensing laws exist to ensure that health workers have the proper training and are:","qualified to practice",["well-paid","famous","wealthy"],"Licensure protects the public.")
H('461.d.9.A',3,"A patient decides on her own which treatment to accept after hearing the options. This is an example of:","autonomy",["neglect","pressure","isolation"],"Autonomy means self-determination.")
H('461.d.9.A',4,"A patient chooses not to have a procedure after a clear explanation of the risks. The health worker should respect the patient's:","right to decide",["wishes only if the family agrees","need for punishment","ability to pay"],"Respect autonomy.")
H('461.d.9.B',3,"Getting vaccines and washing hands are wellness strategies that help prevent:","disease",["homework","traffic","rain"],"Prevention reduces illness.")
H('461.d.9.B',4,"Regular screenings, such as a blood pressure check, are used to find problems early, which supports the prevention of:","serious disease",["good sleep","exercise","hydration"],"Early detection saves lives.")
H('461.d.9.C',3,"A supportive friend who encourages exercise has a positive effect on a person's physical and mental health. A relationship that adds constant stress can have a:","negative effect",["positive effect","no effect ever","pleasant effect"],"Relationships affect health.")
H('461.d.9.C',4,"Being isolated for a long time can increase the risk of depression. This shows the effect of relationships on:","mental health",["weather","finances only","road safety"],"Social ties matter.")
H('461.d.9.D',3,"A patient's bill of rights tells patients they have the right to respectful care and to know the:","risks of treatment",["staff schedules","hospital mascots","cost of supplies"],"Rights protect patients.")
H('461.d.9.D',4,"An advance directive documents what kind of care a person wants if she can no longer speak for herself. It records her:","choices",["bill","school record","phone number"],"Directives record wishes.")
H('461.d.9.E',3,"A hospital serves patients of many backgrounds, so staff learn about different customs, diets, and beliefs. This shows an understanding of:","diversity",["uniformity","isolation","competition"],"Diversity affects care.")
H('461.d.9.E',4,"A patient's religion forbids certain foods. A good health worker will accommodate the diet whenever it is:","medically safe",["too inconvenient","unusual","loud"],"Respect cultural practice.")
H('461.d.10.A',3,"The World Health Organization and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention are examples of:","regulatory and health agencies",["sports leagues","restaurants","game companies"],"These agencies set health guidance.")
H('461.d.10.A',4,"OSHA is a government agency that sets rules to keep health workers safe on the:","job",["stage","bus","field trip only"],"OSHA protects workers.")
H('461.d.10.B',3,"Wearing gloves and washing hands between patients follow industry safety standards called:","standard precautions",["hospital menus","parking rules","dress codes"],"Standard precautions prevent infection.")
H('461.d.10.B',4,"A rule that every hospital must have clear exit routes and working extinguishers is a standard for fire:","safety",["decorating","billing","parking"],"Safety rules include fire safety.")
H('461.d.10.C',3,"Using a sharps container for used needles protects workers and patients from:","injury and infection",["boredom","noise","hunger"],"Safe disposal prevents harm.")
H('461.d.10.C',4,"A health worker who reports a spill in a hallway right away and puts up a warning sign prevents:","falls",["hunger","late bills","long meetings"],"Hazard reporting prevents accidents.")
H('461.d.11.A',3,"Hospitals use equipment such as ultrasound machines, heart monitors, and ventilators in diagnostic and:","therapeutic care",["marketing","sports","cooking"],"Technology aids diagnosis and treatment.")
H('461.d.11.A',4,"An electrocardiogram machine records the heart's electrical activity, so it is used mainly to:","diagnose heart problems",["clean floors","cook meals","wash laundry"],"Different devices serve different tasks.")
H('461.d.11.B',3,"A monitor shows an error code and gives odd readings. A health worker should suspect a possible:","equipment malfunction",["new patient","staff meeting","lunch break"],"Odd readings may indicate a problem.")
H('461.d.11.B',4,"A smoking smell and sparks from a medical device are signs of a malfunction that can endanger patients and staff, so the device should be:","taken out of use",["used faster","covered up","ignored"],"Safety comes first.")
H('461.d.11.C',3,"If a device is not working correctly, a health worker should follow the facility's process by reporting it to a:","supervisor or biomedical staff",["patient's visitor","stranger","competitor"],"Reports go through proper channels.")
H('461.d.11.C',4,"Documenting what happened with a faulty device, with the date and equipment number, helps the facility to:","track and fix problems",["avoid training","hide the problem","raise prices"],"Reports support repair and safety.")

# ---- 462 Biotechnology ----
H('462.d.1.A',3,"A student who enjoys lab work and plant science visits a seed company to see what biotechnology workers do. This visit is a way to determine:","interest in the field",["a grade level","a tax rate","a bus route"],"Exploration reveals interests.")
H('462.d.1.A',4,"Job shadowing a lab technician helps a student learn whether the daily tasks match his:","interests and abilities",["wardrobe","phone plan","lunch order"],"Experience guides decisions.")
H('462.d.1.B',3,"Quality control analyst, research technician, and fermentation operator are all jobs found in:","biotechnology",["shipping only","retail only","farming only"],"Many careers exist in biotech.")
H('462.d.1.B',4,"A student who wants a career testing the purity of vaccines would look at jobs in:","quality control",["sports marketing","fashion design","food service only"],"Quality control tests products.")
H('462.d.1.C',3,"To find accurate information on pay and training for biotechnology careers, a student should check a government labor site or a:","professional organization website",["gossip blog","random video","advertisement"],"Reliable sources provide accurate data.")
H('462.d.1.C',4,"A career source is more reliable when it names the author, gives a date, and cites its:","sources of data",["favorite color","bank balance","mascot"],"Credible sources are documented.")
H('462.d.1.D',3,"A student writes a short summary of her skills, education plans, and career goals in biotechnology. This helps her:","communicate her qualifications",["avoid school","skip research","hide her interests"],"Self-description supports applications.")
H('462.d.1.D',4,"A student who tells an advisor that she excels at lab math and plans on a two-year degree is communicating her knowledge and:","educational level",["birthday","street address","favorite song"],"Advisors need these details.")
H('462.d.1.E',3,"A lab technician job is conventional, while a job that combines biology with art, such as science illustration, is a:","non-conventional opportunity",["required class","mandatory test","school rule"],"Unusual careers also use biotech knowledge.")
H('462.d.1.E',4,"A woman who is a scientist and wants to teach science to children may find opportunities in a:","non-conventional career",["standard laboratory only","factory line only","retail store only"],"Careers can be blended.")
H('462.d.1.F',3,"Using bacteria to make insulin is a biotechnology application in:","medicine",["music","sports","fashion"],"Biotech makes medical products.")
H('462.d.1.F',4,"Microbes that clean up an oil spill are an application of biotechnology to the:","environment",["stage","courtroom","playground"],"Bioremediation helps the environment.")
H('462.d.1.G',3,"A student searching a science database must evaluate whether a source is credible. A source is more reliable if it was:","peer reviewed",["posted anonymously","unsigned","an advertisement"],"Peer review checks quality.")
H('462.d.1.G',4,"When researching a topic online, a student should compare information from several sources to check for:","accuracy and bias",["colors","fonts","speed"],"Cross-checking reduces error.")
H('462.d.1.H',3,"A student reads an article in an academic journal. These articles report original research and are usually reviewed by other:","scientists",["actors","coaches","chefs"],"Peer review is by experts.")
H('462.d.1.H',4,"To read a scientific article critically, a student should look for the question, methods, results, and the:","conclusion",["advertisement","crossword","menu"],"Articles follow a structure.")
H('462.d.2.A',3,"Debates about genetically modified foods and the use of human genetic data raise current ethical and legal:","issues",["menus","holidays","costumes"],"Biotech raises hard questions.")
H('462.d.2.A',4,"Deciding who owns the rights to a gene sequence is a legal question, while deciding whether it is right to alter embryos is an:","ethical question",["tax question","weather question","scheduling question"],"Law and ethics both matter.")
H('462.d.2.B',3,"Early farmers practiced selective breeding long before DNA was understood. Biotechnology therefore has a long:","history",["menu","price","speed limit"],"Biotech began with breeding and fermentation.")
H('462.d.2.B',4,"The announcement of the cloned sheep Dolly raised public concern about the ethics of:","cloning",["recycling","tourism","furniture"],"Cloning triggered debate.")
H('462.d.2.C',3,"Two biotechnology topics, such as gene therapy and genetically modified crops, each involve legal and technology issues. A student who compares them is discussing the topics' legal and:","technology concerns",["spelling concerns","color concerns","music concerns"],"Both law and technology shape biotech.")
H('462.d.2.C',4,"A patent gives an inventor exclusive rights to a new biotechnology process for a set time. A patent is a:","legal protection",["tax","recipe","grade"],"Patents protect inventions.")
H('462.d.2.D',3,"A claim about a new gene therapy is supported by lab data and measurements. Evidence that can be measured is called:","objective evidence",["personal feeling","rumor","opinion"],"Objective evidence is measurable.")
H('462.d.2.D',4,"A person's feeling that a food is unsafe, without test data, is a view supported by:","subjective evidence",["objective evidence","peer review","controlled trials"],"Personal belief is subjective.")
H('462.d.3.A',3,"The Food and Drug Administration, the Environmental Protection Agency, and the Department of Agriculture are agencies that regulate:","biotechnology products",["video games","fashion","sports"],"Federal agencies oversee biotech.")
H('462.d.3.A',4,"A company that wants to sell a new drug made with biotechnology must have it approved by the:","FDA",["IRS","NASA","NFL"],"The FDA approves drugs.")
H('462.d.3.B',3,"The Biotechnology Innovation Organization represents companies in the industry and helps shape:","policy and standards",["school lunch","bus schedules","fashion trends"],"Groups influence rules.")
H('462.d.3.B',4,"Professional organizations help set guidelines that biotechnology labs follow to keep work:","safe and ethical",["secret","slow","expensive"],"Standards guide practice.")
H('462.d.3.C',3,"Rules that say work must be done in a documented, consistent way, such as good laboratory practices, are called:","regulations",["suggestions","rumors","jokes"],"Regulations set requirements.")
H('462.d.3.C',4,"GMP stands for good manufacturing practice, which means products are made and checked in a way that ensures their:","quality and safety",["color","cost","speed"],"GMP ensures consistent quality.")
H('462.d.3.D',3,"A lab keeps a written step-by-step procedure for each test so every technician follows the same method. These are called:","standard operating procedures",["school rules","weather reports","menus"],"SOPs keep results consistent.")
H('462.d.3.D',4,"A technician records the date, sample, and result of each test in a lab notebook so that the work can be:","reviewed and repeated",["forgotten","hidden","sold"],"Records support quality.")
H('462.d.4.A',3,"The journals Nature and Science are examples of professional:","publications",["clubs","games","stores"],"Journals share research.")
H('462.d.4.A',4,"A professional publication for biotechnology workers may include articles about new techniques, news about the industry, and:","job announcements",["music lyrics","game scores","clothing ads"],"Industry publications cover jobs and news.")
H('462.d.4.B',3,"Companies that make crops, those that make medicines, and those that make industrial enzymes are different biotechnology industry:","sectors",["holidays","hobbies","colors"],"Biotech has many sectors.")
H('462.d.4.B',4,"A company producing biofuels from algae belongs to the biotechnology sector of:","industrial or energy biotechnology",["fashion retail","banking","sports media"],"Biofuel is an industrial application.")
H('462.d.4.C',3,"A student studies the training, pay, and demand for a lab technician job and shares the findings in a short report. She is investigating and reporting on:","career opportunities",["sports leagues","music genres","shopping malls"],"Career research guides plans.")
H('462.d.4.C',4,"The Occupational Outlook Handbook lists job outlook, pay, and:","required education",["favorite foods","vacation spots","team colors"],"Handbooks list requirements.")
H('462.d.4.D',3,"Joining HOSA or a local biotechnology club lets a student meet professionals and practice skills through:","a professional organization",["a bank","a shop","a hotel"],"Clubs connect students to the field.")
H('462.d.4.D',4,"A state biotechnology association offers networking events that help members find:","jobs and mentors",["video games","fashion","restaurants"],"Networking opens doors.")
H('462.d.5.A',3,"A lab technician writes a clear email, speaks politely on the phone, and listens during a meeting. These are examples of:","communication skills",["lab techniques","cooking skills","driving skills"],"Communication takes many forms.")
H('462.d.5.A',4,"A worker uses email and a shared online document to send results to a team member in another city. This is:","electronic communication",["a face-to-face talk","a letter by post","a phone call by wire"],"Electronic tools connect teams.")
H('462.d.5.B',3,"For a lab job interview, a good applicant brings a resume, dresses neatly, and arrives:","early",["late","after lunch","next week"],"Interview skills help secure jobs.")
H('462.d.5.B',4,"Showing up on time, following directions, and learning new tasks help a worker to:","keep a job",["lose a job","skip training","avoid feedback"],"Good habits maintain employment.")
H('462.d.5.C',3,"Greeting coworkers politely and respecting their space and time are examples of workplace:","etiquette",["secrecy","rivalry","jargon"],"Etiquette shows respect.")
H('462.d.5.C',4,"Keeping a phone silent during a meeting and not interrupting others show good:","workplace manners",["laziness","pride","noise"],"Manners support a positive environment.")
H('462.d.5.D',3,"A technician who stays focused, finishes tasks on time, and asks for help when stuck shows productive:","work habits",["rumors","excuses","delays"],"Habits drive productivity.")
H('462.d.5.D',4,"A positive attitude at work includes accepting feedback and being willing to:","learn new things",["quit quickly","blame others","avoid tasks"],"Positive attitude supports growth.")
H('462.d.5.E',3,"Wearing goggles, gloves, and a lab coat while handling chemicals are examples of safety:","equipment",["entertainment","decorations","souvenirs"],"PPE protects workers.")
H('462.d.5.E',4,"Texas workers can learn about their right to a safe job from the:","Texas Workforce Commission and OSHA",["school cafeteria","local theater","sports network"],"Safety rules come from agencies.")
H('462.d.6.A',3,"Brewing beer uses yeast to ferment sugars. The yeast is a living organism that changes the sugars into alcohol and carbon dioxide. This is a biotechnology:","manufacturing process",["sports event","board game","fashion show"],"Fermentation is a classic process.")
H('462.d.6.A',4,"Producing insulin in engineered bacteria is a process whose end product is a:","medicine",["fuel","fabric","toy"],"Biotech produces drugs.")
H('462.d.6.B',3,"If a biotechnology plant dumps untreated waste into a stream, living things in the stream and nonliving factors such as water pH can be:","harmed",["improved","unchanged always","entertained"],"Waste impacts ecosystems.")
H('462.d.6.B',4,"Waste that raises the temperature of a lake can reduce the oxygen available to fish. Temperature is an example of an:","abiotic factor",["biotic factor","food chain","predator"],"Temperature is nonliving.")
H('462.d.6.C',3,"Biotech companies analyze the leftover materials from production, such as spent fermentation broth, to decide how to safely handle the:","refuse",["sales","hiring","mascot"],"Refuse analysis guides disposal.")
H('462.d.6.C',4,"Testing manufacturing waste for toxins before release helps a company to follow:","environmental regulations",["fashion trends","game rules","lunch menus"],"Testing ensures compliance.")
H('462.d.6.D',3,"Too much waste can harm a person's health, a community's water supply, and the broader:","environment",["lunchroom","hallway","playground"],"Waste affects many levels.")
H('462.d.6.D',4,"A factory's waste in a river can harm the individual who drinks the water, the community that relies on it, and the:","ecosystem",["wardrobe","weekend","menu"],"Impacts extend from one person to nature.")
H('462.d.6.E',3,"Bacteria that eat oil spilled in soil are used to clean it up. This solution uses living organisms and is called:","bioremediation",["bioluminescence","biofuel","bioethics"],"Microbes clean pollution.")
H('462.d.6.E',4,"A company using plants to remove metals from contaminated soil is also an example of a:","bioremediation solution",["marketing plan","sports drill","tax credit"],"Phytoremediation is one type.")
H('462.d.6.F',3,"Laws that limit what companies can release into air and water support waste management by requiring:","permits and monitoring",["more waste","less testing","no records"],"Regulations enforce management.")
H('462.d.6.F',4,"Evidence that recycling and treatment lower pollution is used to support waste management:","policies",["games","menus","hobbies"],"Policies rely on evidence.")
H('462.d.7.A',3,"Developing crops that resist insects through selective breeding or gene transfer is an application of:","agricultural biotechnology",["medical biotechnology","space technology","marine biology only"],"Ag biotech improves crops.")
H('462.d.7.A',4,"Drought-resistant corn is an example of a crop improved through:","biotechnology",["weather control","road building","clothing design"],"Traits are enhanced.")
H('462.d.7.B',3,"Making cheese, yogurt, and bread with microbes is an example of fermented food production in:","industrial biotechnology",["sports medicine","architecture","law enforcement"],"Fermentation makes foods.")
H('462.d.7.B',4,"Enzymes added to laundry detergent to break down stains are an example of an industrial:","biotechnology product",["sports drink","road sign","mineral"],"Industrial enzymes are used in many products.")
H('462.d.7.C',3,"Vaccines, antibiotics, and insulin are examples of products from medical and:","pharmaceutical biotechnology",["fashion design","road building","film editing"],"Drugs result from biotech.")
H('462.d.7.C',4,"Monoclonal antibodies used to treat some cancers are made using biotechnology, so they are examples of:","medical applications",["farm tools","toys","clothing"],"Modern therapies use biotech.")
H('462.d.7.D',3,"Sequencing the DNA of a virus to understand how it spreads is an example of:","research and development",["marketing","accounting","landscaping"],"Research drives innovation.")
H('462.d.7.D',4,"A research team that develops a new test to detect disease from a drop of blood is performing biotechnology:","research and development",["sales","retail","shipping"],"R and D creates new tools.")
H('462.d.7.E',3,"Analyzing DNA from a crime scene to match a suspect is an application of biotechnology in:","forensics",["fashion","music","cooking"],"DNA profiling aids investigation.")
H('462.d.7.E',4,"Using genetic tests to identify a species of fish being sold in a market is an application in:","food and environmental science",["fashion design","sports","architecture"],"DNA barcoding confirms species.")
H('462.d.7.F',3,"Before a genetically modified crop can be sold, companies must follow ethical considerations, laws, and:","regulations",["wishes","guesses","rumors"],"Laws govern release.")
H('462.d.7.F',4,"Labeling rules for foods made with biotechnology are examples of:","regulations",["suggestions","advertisements","jokes"],"Labels follow rules.")
H('462.d.7.G',3,"A compound light microscope is used in a biotechnology lab to magnify:","cells and microorganisms",["buildings","mountains","vehicles"],"Microscopes show tiny things.")
H('462.d.7.G',4,"A centrifuge spins samples at high speed to separate their parts by:","density",["color","weight of the tube","cost"],"Centrifugation separates mixtures.")

# ---- 472 Pharmacy Technician ----
H('472.d.1.A',3,"Ancient Greek medicine, led by Hippocrates around 440 BC, started to explain illness through natural causes rather than only through:","gods or spirits",["math","music","maps"],"Hippocrates shifted thinking.")
H('472.d.1.A',4,"The belief that illness came from imbalances of four fluids, called humors, was a major idea in medicine for roughly:","two thousand years",["two days","two weeks","two minutes"],"Humoral theory lasted for centuries.")
H('472.d.1.B',3,"In earlier centuries, illness was often blamed on curses or angry spirits. These are called:","supernatural explanations",["scientific explanations","legal explanations","economic explanations"],"Supernatural beliefs once guided care.")
H('472.d.1.B',4,"Healers who believed illness had spiritual causes might use prayers, charms, and:","herbs",["microscopes","antibiotics","vaccines"],"Early treatments used plants and rituals.")
H('472.d.1.C',3,"During the Enlightenment, anatomists and scientists used observation and experiments to learn how the body works. This approach is called the:","scientific method",["lucky guess","tradition only","rumor"],"Enlightenment valued reason.")
H('472.d.1.C',4,"The invention of the microscope in the 1600s let scientists see tiny organisms for the first time, a key advance of the:","Enlightenment era",["Stone Age","Bronze Age","Space Age"],"Instruments aided discovery.")
H('472.d.1.D',3,"A common medical practice of the 1700s and 1800s that removed blood from patients to try to cure illness was:","bloodletting",["vaccination","dialysis","imaging"],"Bloodletting was widespread.")
H('472.d.1.D',4,"Edward Jenner's smallpox vaccine in 1796 started the field of:","vaccination",["bloodletting","surgery by saw","herbal tea"],"Vaccines began with Jenner.")
H('472.d.1.E',3,"The introduction of penicillin in the 1940s changed medicine in the United States because it could treat many:","bacterial infections",["broken bones","hearing problems","vision problems"],"Antibiotics saved lives.")
H('472.d.1.E',4,"The Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act of 1938 required drugs to be proved safe before they could be:","sold to the public",["advertised for free","grown on farms","made at home only"],"Safety rules followed tragedies.")
H('472.d.2.A',3,"A technician must follow state and federal laws. In Texas, the agency that licenses pharmacists and regulates their practice is the Texas State Board of:","Pharmacy",["Music","Sports","Tourism"],"The board enforces pharmacy law.")
H('472.d.2.A',4,"The Controlled Substances Act controls drugs that can be abused, such as opioids, by classifying them into:","schedules",["menus","chapters","brands"],"Drugs are scheduled by abuse risk.")
H('472.d.2.B',3,"A pharmacist fills a prescription with the wrong drug and a patient is harmed. This could lead to a claim of medical:","malpractice",["generosity","teamwork","charity"],"Malpractice involves harm from errors.")
H('472.d.2.B',4,"A mistake in giving a drug that was caused by a failure to use reasonable care is called:","negligence",["accuracy","kindness","luck"],"Negligence is failure to use care.")
H('472.d.2.C',3,"A drug maker is sued because a defective medicine harmed users. This kind of claim is called:","product liability",["patient privacy","copyright","advertising"],"Product liability covers defects.")
H('472.d.2.C',4,"If a patient does not follow directions and is also harmed, the law may consider the patient partly at fault, which is called:","contributory negligence",["malpractice","assault","slander"],"Fault can be shared.")
H('472.d.2.D',3,"A pharmacist may counsel patients and verify prescriptions, but a technician is not allowed to give:","professional judgment or advice about drug therapy",["labels","stock","counts"],"Roles differ by licensure.")
H('472.d.2.D',4,"A technician counts pills and prepares a label, and the pharmacist then performs the final:","check of the prescription",["delivery","advertising","cleaning"],"Pharmacists verify.")
H('472.d.2.E',3,"Pharmacists help manage opioid therapy by checking prescriptions, watching for misuse, and educating patients on safe:","storage and disposal",["advertising","painting","parking"],"Safe handling reduces misuse.")
H('472.d.2.E',4,"A pharmacist who notices a patient getting several opioid prescriptions from different doctors may contact the prescribers to address a risk of:","overdose or misuse",["bad weather","low sales","slow service"],"Monitoring protects patients.")
H('472.d.2.F',3,"A technician must never share a customer's prescription information with someone who is not authorized, because patient information is:","confidential",["public","free","advertised"],"Confidentiality is essential.")
H('472.d.2.F',4,"Leaving a customer's printed prescription records on an open counter violates the duty to maintain:","privacy",["inventory","schedules","sales"],"Records must be secured.")
H('472.d.2.G',3,"A wrongful act that causes harm to another person, which can be the basis of a civil lawsuit, is called a:","tort",["ballot","budget","vote"],"Torts are civil wrongs.")
H('472.d.2.G',4,"HIPAA is related to medical negligence because releasing records without permission can be a violation that harms the patient's:","privacy rights",["parking","schedule","meal plan"],"HIPAA protects privacy.")
H('472.d.2.H',3,"Professional liability insurance protects a pharmacist or technician if a patient claims a mistake caused:","injury",["profit","joy","growth"],"Liability covers claims of harm.")
H('472.d.3.A',3,"A pharmacy technician at work keeps hair tied back, wears a clean lab coat, and uses closed-toe shoes. This is appropriate:","professional attire",["costume","beachwear","party wear"],"Attire protects safety and image.")
H('472.d.3.A',4,"Clean, neat uniforms in a pharmacy help prevent contamination of medicines and build patient:","confidence",["fear","anger","boredom"],"Appearance builds trust.")
H('472.d.3.B',3,"Washing hands before handling medicines is an example of expected personal:","hygiene",["style","hobbies","finances"],"Hygiene prevents contamination.")
H('472.d.3.B',4,"A pharmacy employee with a cold should stay home or wear a mask because germs could contaminate the:","medications",["parking lot","wall paint","lobby music"],"Illness risks contamination.")
H('472.d.3.C',3,"A pharmacy technician who is polite, dependable, and honest shows professional:","attitudes and behaviors",["avoidance","laziness","rudeness"],"Professionalism is expected.")
H('472.d.3.C',4,"Arriving on time, staying focused, and respecting patients are ways to show:","professionalism",["boredom","tardiness","distraction"],"These behaviors build trust.")
H('472.d.3.D',3,"Speaking clearly, listening, and checking understanding are characteristics of effective communication, while mumbling and ignoring questions are characteristics of:","ineffective communication",["teamwork","leadership","accuracy"],"Behavior affects communication.")
H('472.d.3.D',4,"A technician who repeats a patient's question back to be sure she understood is showing a trait of:","effective communication",["ineffective communication","avoidance","carelessness"],"Clarifying helps accuracy.")
H('472.d.3.E',3,"A prescription says bid. Knowing that this abbreviation means twice daily, the technician correctly reads and communicates:","medical vocabulary",["slang","jokes","riddles"],"Abbreviations must be accurate.")
H('472.d.3.E',4,"Translating the abbreviation prn on a label into plain words for a patient, which means as needed, shows the ability to:","communicate medical vocabulary",["sell medicine","order supplies","clean shelves"],"Technicians must be clear.")
H('472.d.3.F',3,"A noisy pharmacy makes it hard for a patient to hear counseling. One way to remove this barrier is to move to a:","quiet private area",["louder spot","busier counter","outer lobby"],"Reduce noise and distraction.")
H('472.d.3.F',4,"A patient does not understand a drug label written in complex words. A helpful way to remove this barrier is to use:","plain language",["larger words","longer sentences","more jargon"],"Plain language aids understanding.")
H('472.d.3.G',3,"For a patient who is hard of hearing, a technician can face the patient, speak clearly, and provide information in:","writing",["whispers","fast speech","a different room"],"Adapt to the person.")
H('472.d.3.G',4,"A customer with limited English needs help. The technician should ask for a qualified:","interpreter",["decorator","salesperson","driver"],"Interpreters help communication.")
H('472.d.4.A',3,"Planning tasks, setting priorities, and handling interruptions are examples of time management, and breathing exercises and breaks are examples of:","stress management",["inventory control","pricing","billing"],"Both help performance.")
H('472.d.4.A',4,"When a pharmacy begins using new software, the technician learns the system and adjusts. This is called:","change management",["time travel","delay","inventory"],"Change requires adaptation.")
H('472.d.4.B',3,"Negotiation, empathy, and cooperation are examples of:","interpersonal skills",["laboratory skills","math skills","driving skills"],"People skills matter.")
H('472.d.4.B',4,"A technician who disagrees with a coworker over a work schedule uses negotiation by:","finding a solution both can accept",["refusing to talk","demanding to win","complaining to patients"],"Negotiation seeks agreement.")
H('472.d.4.C',3,"When a prescription label is missing information, the technician finds out what is needed and follows the right steps to fix it. This is:","problem-solving",["avoidance","delay","denial"],"Problem-solving needs a plan.")
H('472.d.4.C',4,"After a recurring error in label printing, the pharmacy changes its checking process. This shows implementing an effective:","solution",["mistake","delay","complaint"],"Solutions prevent repeats.")
H('472.d.4.D',3,"The Texas State Board of Pharmacy sets the minimum standards of practice that pharmacy workers must:","meet",["avoid","argue","ignore"],"Standards define the minimum.")
H('472.d.4.D',4,"A pharmacy that does not follow the board's rules for safe storage could face:","disciplinary action",["a bonus","a holiday","a raise"],"Violations bring penalties.")
H('472.d.4.E',3,"Taking continuing education courses and keeping certification current are ways to maintain:","competency",["inventory","salary","hours"],"Learning keeps skills current.")
H('472.d.4.E',4,"Because new drugs and rules appear often, a technician keeps his skills current through training and:","professional organizations",["time off","long lunches","rumors"],"Organizations offer updates.")
H('472.d.4.F',3,"Pharmacist, pharmacy technician, and pharmacy buyer are different:","career paths in pharmacy",["colors","countries","seasons"],"Many roles exist.")
H('472.d.4.F',4,"A technician who wants to become a pharmacist would need to earn a:","doctor of pharmacy degree",["driver's license","food permit","barber license"],"Pharmacists need a PharmD.")
H('472.d.5.A',3,"A pill swallowed by mouth is given by the oral route, while a medicine put under the tongue is given by the:","sublingual route",["topical route","rectal route","nasal route"],"Routes describe how drugs enter.")
H('472.d.5.A',4,"A medicine given by needle into a vein is given by the intravenous route, which sends the drug into the:","bloodstream",["stomach","skin","lungs"],"IV acts quickly.")
H('472.d.5.B',3,"Antibiotics, analgesics, and antihypertensives are different:","classes of drugs",["brands","sizes","colors"],"Classes group drugs by use.")
H('472.d.5.B',4,"A drug used to treat infection caused by bacteria belongs to the class called:","antibiotics",["analgesics","antihistamines","diuretics"],"Antibiotics fight bacteria.")
H('472.d.5.C',3,"In the term gastritis, the root gastr refers to the stomach and the suffix itis means:","inflammation",["removal","study","pain"],"Suffixes carry meaning.")
H('472.d.5.C',4,"The abbreviation qd on older prescriptions means once a day, and the prefix hypo means:","under or below normal",["above normal","before","after"],"Word parts guide meaning.")
H('472.d.5.D',3,"The term for how a drug is absorbed, distributed, and removed by the body is:","pharmacokinetics",["pharmacy law","anatomy","inventory"],"Kinetics tracks the drug's path.")
H('472.d.5.D',4,"A side effect is an unintended effect of a drug, while the intended benefit is its:","therapeutic effect",["adverse reaction","allergy","overdose"],"Terms differ by intent.")
H('472.d.5.E',3,"A technician sees a new drug name, antiemetic. Knowing that anti means against and emesis means vomiting, she can figure out that it:","prevents vomiting",["causes vomiting","raises blood sugar","lowers pain"],"Word parts reveal meaning.")
H('472.d.5.E',4,"Seeing the suffix -itis in a drug use statement lets a technician guess that the drug treats:","inflammation",["infection only","pain only","thirst"],"Roots help understanding.")
H('472.d.6.A',3,"A pharmacy technician converts 2 tablespoons to teaspoons using 1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons. The result is:","6 teaspoons",["2 teaspoons","3 teaspoons","9 teaspoons"],"2 x 3 = 6.")
H('472.d.6.A',4,"A medicine order calls for 750 mg of a drug supplied in 250 mg tablets. The number of tablets needed is:","3",["2","4","5"],"750 / 250 = 3.")
H('472.d.6.B',3,"A syringe holds 5 mL. Since 1 L = 1,000 mL, the amount in liters is:","0.005 L",["0.5 L","5 L","0.05 L"],"5 / 1,000 = 0.005.")
H('472.d.6.B',4,"A dose of 2.5 g converted to milligrams is:","2,500 mg",["25 mg","250 mg","25,000 mg"],"1 g = 1,000 mg.")
H('472.d.6.C',3,"A patient weighs 110 pounds. Using 1 kg = 2.2 lb, the weight in kilograms is:","50 kg",["242 kg","25 kg","100 kg"],"110 / 2.2 = 50.")
H('472.d.6.C',4,"Using 1 grain = 65 mg, a 5 grain tablet contains how many milligrams?","325 mg",["13 mg","65 mg","650 mg"],"5 x 65 = 325.")
H('472.d.6.D',3,"A drug is 20 mg per mL. To give a 60 mg dose, the volume needed is:","3 mL",["1 mL","6 mL","30 mL"],"60 / 20 = 3.")
H('472.d.6.D',4,"A solution contains 500 mg in 250 mL. The concentration in mg per mL is:","2 mg/mL",["0.5 mg/mL","125 mg/mL","750 mg/mL"],"500 / 250 = 2.")
H('472.d.7.A',3,"The heart and blood vessels make up the circulatory system, and the lungs are part of the:","respiratory system",["digestive system","skeletal system","nervous system"],"Body systems have distinct parts.")
H('472.d.7.A',4,"The organ system that removes waste from the blood and makes urine is the:","urinary system",["nervous system","endocrine system","muscular system"],"Kidneys filter blood.")
H('472.d.7.B',3,"A disease process in which the airways narrow and make breathing hard, such as asthma, affects the:","respiratory system",["digestive system","skin","skeleton"],"Pathophysiology links disease to systems.")
H('472.d.7.B',4,"High blood pressure that damages arteries over time is a pathology of the:","cardiovascular system",["urinary system","skeletal system","nervous system only"],"Hypertension harms vessels.")
H('472.d.7.C',3,"Diuretics, which help the body remove extra fluid, affect the:","kidneys and urinary system",["bones","skin only","eyes"],"Drugs target systems.")
H('472.d.7.C',4,"Bronchodilators, which open the airways, are a drug category that affects the:","respiratory system",["urinary system","skeletal system","digestive system"],"Each category acts on a system.")
H('472.d.8.A',3,"A pharmacist who gives flu shots follows a schedule of recommended vaccines that depends on a person's:","age and health",["favorite color","address","hobbies"],"Schedules guide timing.")
H('472.d.8.A',4,"Counseling a parent about when a child should receive each vaccine is following the recommended:","immunization schedule",["grocery list","bus route","dress code"],"Schedules are published by health authorities.")
H('472.d.8.B',3,"Some people are exempt from certain vaccines for medical reasons, such as a severe allergy, or for religious or conscientious:","beliefs",["games","hobbies","recipes"],"Exemptions have categories.")
H('472.d.8.B',4,"A medical exemption from a vaccine usually requires a note from a licensed:","health provider",["neighbor","coach","reporter"],"Providers certify medical reasons.")
H('472.d.8.C',3,"After a vaccine is given, the provider records the vaccine name, the lot number, the date, and the site of the shot. This is:","documentation",["advertising","accounting","shipping"],"Records are required.")
H('472.d.8.C',4,"Storing vaccines at the right temperature is a standard step because heat or cold can make them:","less effective",["tastier","louder","brighter"],"Cold chain protects vaccines.")
H('472.d.8.D',3,"A report system collects data on possible harm after a vaccine so scientists can analyze whether the vaccine caused the:","adverse event",["holiday","tradition","sale"],"Data helps analyze safety.")
H('472.d.8.D',4,"When reading data on vaccine injuries, a careful student looks at how many people were vaccinated and how rare the:","reactions are",["colors are","brands are","stores are"],"Rates matter in safety data.")
H('472.d.8.E',3,"Herbal supplements and acupuncture are examples of complementary and alternative medicine. Evaluating them requires looking at:","scientific evidence",["advertising slogans","personal opinions only","popularity alone"],"Evidence determines effectiveness.")
H('472.d.8.E',4,"A supplement may interact with a prescription drug, so patients should tell their pharmacist about every:","product they take",["place they shop","friend they have","song they like"],"Interactions are a safety risk.")
H('472.d.8.F',3,"Checking blood pressure and cholesterol at regular intervals helps find problems early. These are examples of:","health screenings",["advertisements","fundraisers","holidays"],"Screenings detect issues.")
H('472.d.8.F',4,"Public health programs that offer free screenings aim to keep a population healthier by finding disease:","early",["late","never","randomly"],"Early detection improves outcomes.")
H('472.d.8.G',3,"Diet, exercise, sleep, and smoking are external factors that affect a person's:","health",["birthday","address","hair color"],"Lifestyle shapes health.")
H('472.d.8.G',4,"A patient with high blood pressure who exercises and eats less salt may need a lower dose of medication because lifestyle factors can improve:","drug response and health",["parking","mood only","spelling"],"Lifestyle interacts with therapy.")
H('472.d.8.H',3,"A pharmacist who reviews all of a patient's medicines to make sure they work well together and are used correctly is providing:","medication therapy management",["customer parking","inventory counts","store marketing"],"MTM improves therapy outcomes.")
H('472.d.8.H',4,"Medication therapy management can reduce hospital visits by finding problems such as duplicate drugs and missed:","doses",["colors","sizes","logos"],"MTM improves adherence and safety.")
H('472.d.9.A',3,"The agency that sets and enforces workplace safety rules in the United States is the:","Occupational Safety and Health Administration",["Food and Drug Administration","Department of Education","Postal Service"],"OSHA protects workers.")
H('472.d.9.A',4,"OSHA requires employers to train workers about the hazards of chemicals and to provide:","protective equipment",["bonuses","vacations","parking"],"Employers must protect workers.")
H('472.d.9.B',3,"NIOSH recommends safe handling practices for hazardous drugs because exposure can harm workers' health. NIOSH stands for the National Institute for Occupational:","Safety and Health",["Study and Housing","Sales and Hiring","Safety and Hunting"],"NIOSH researches worker safety.")
H('472.d.9.B',4,"NIOSH maintains a list of hazardous drugs that need special handling because they can cause:","harm to workers",["higher sales","faster service","cheaper bills"],"The list guides precautions.")
H('472.d.9.C',3,"USP chapters set standards for compounding sterile preparations in order to prevent:","contamination of medicines",["slow service","low sales","lost keys"],"USP rules protect patients.")
H('472.d.9.C',4,"The abbreviation USP stands for United States:","Pharmacopeia",["Postal Service","Pharmacy","Professionals"],"USP sets quality standards.")
H('472.d.9.D',3,"A chemotherapy drug is a hazardous medication, so a technician handling it should wear special gloves and a gown and follow rules for safe:","disposal",["advertising","pricing","staging"],"Hazardous drugs need protection.")
H('472.d.9.D',4,"Cleaning up a spill of a hazardous drug should be done with a spill kit, while wearing proper:","protective equipment",["perfume","jewelry","headphones"],"Spills require PPE.")
H('472.d.9.E',3,"Bloodborne pathogens such as hepatitis B and HIV can be spread through contact with infected blood. Workers prevent exposure by using standard:","precautions",["fashions","habits","discounts"],"Precautions reduce transmission.")
H('472.d.9.E',4,"A technician who is stuck by a used needle should wash the area and immediately report it to a:","supervisor",["customer","neighbor","friend"],"Prompt reporting enables treatment.")
H('472.d.9.F',3,"The Hazard Communication Standard requires labels on hazardous chemicals and access to safety data sheets, which help workers know a chemical's:","hazards",["prices","brands","colors"],"HazCom informs workers.")
H('472.d.9.F',4,"A safety data sheet for a cleaning chemical tells workers how to use it safely and what to do in an:","emergency",["advertisement","audit","election"],"SDSs give emergency steps.")

H('472.d.2.H',4,"Malpractice insurance is one form of professional liability coverage, which exists because health workers can be held legally responsible for:","errors that injure patients",["the weather","building repairs","holiday schedules"],"Liability means legal responsibility for harm.")

# ---- 474 Mathematics for Health Science ----
H('474.d.1.A',3,"A nurse uses a ratio to figure how much medicine to give a patient from a larger supply. This is applying mathematics to a:","health science problem",["sports score","music lesson","map reading"],"Math supports patient care.")
H('474.d.1.A',4,"A dietitian calculates calories from grams of fat, protein, and carbohydrates. This is using math in a:","health science profession",["fashion shop","film studio","bank vault"],"Math is used across professions.")
H('474.d.1.B',3,"A problem-solving model starts by reading the problem and listing what is given and what is:","asked",["ignored","hidden","guessed"],"Analyze givens first.")
H('474.d.1.B',4,"After solving a medication problem, a good problem solver checks whether the answer is reasonable by:","evaluating the solution",["skipping the check","doubling the answer","guessing again"],"Checking prevents errors.")
H('474.d.1.C',3,"A student uses a calculator and a ruler to solve a measurement problem. Calculators and rulers are examples of:","tools",["problems","answers","units"],"Tools help solve problems.")
H('474.d.1.C',4,"Choosing between mental math, paper and pencil, and a calculator depends on the size and difficulty of the:","calculation",["classroom","teacher","lunch"],"Select the right tool for the task.")
H('474.d.1.D',3,"A student explains her steps for a dosage calculation to a classmate. She is communicating her:","mathematical reasoning",["opinions","hobbies","grades"],"Explaining shows understanding.")
H('474.d.1.D',4,"When a technician writes out each step of a calculation and labels the units, others can see the logic and catch:","errors",["jokes","songs","games"],"Written steps are checkable.")
H('474.d.1.E',3,"A nurse makes a table of a patient's pulse readings across the day. The table helps record and organize:","data",["recipes","rumors","prizes"],"Tables organize information.")
H('474.d.1.E',4,"Drawing a bar graph of the number of flu cases each month represents data in a form that makes it easy to see:","changes over time",["the weather","hospital colors","staff names"],"Graphs communicate patterns.")
H('474.d.1.F',3,"A technician sees that doubling a medicine dose doubles the amount of liquid needed. She has found a mathematical:","relationship",["mistake","coincidence","rumor"],"Proportional relationships connect quantities.")
H('474.d.1.F',4,"Connecting a graph of heart rate to a table of values shows how two ways of representing data are:","related",["unrelated","equal in size","hidden"],"Representations connect.")
H('474.d.1.G',3,"A student justifies a medication answer by showing the formula, the units, and each step in the calculation. This uses:","precise mathematical language",["slang","guesswork","opinions"],"Justification needs clear language.")
H('474.d.1.G',4,"To argue that a dosage plan is correct, a health worker could show how the answer follows from the:","given information",["time of day","room color","lunch menu"],"Arguments rest on facts.")
H('474.d.2.A',3,"A dose is 3/4 of a tablet and the patient takes 2 doses. The total in tablets is:","1 1/2",["3/4","2","2 1/4"],"3/4 x 2 = 1 1/2.")
H('474.d.2.A',4,"A solution holds 0.25 L. After using 0.075 L, the amount left is:","0.175 L",["0.325 L","0.75 L","0.075 L"],"0.25 - 0.075 = 0.175.")
H('474.d.2.B',3,"Under First In, Last Out inventory control, the supplies stocked most recently are used:","before older supplies",["after older supplies","only on weekends","never"],"FILO pulls the newest stock first.")
H('474.d.2.B',4,"Medical supplies with expiration dates are often managed so the earliest-expiring items are used first, which prevents:","waste",["savings","growth","safety"],"Rotation reduces expired stock.")
H('474.d.2.C',3,"A nurse sees 18 patients in 6 hours. The rate in patients per hour is:","3",["6","12","108"],"18 / 6 = 3.")
H('474.d.2.C',4,"A hospital staffs 2 nurses for every 8 patients. For 40 patients the number of nurses needed is:","10",["5","8","16"],"40 / 8 x 2 = 10.")
H('474.d.2.D',3,"In military time, 2:30 PM is written as:","1430",["0230","2030","1230"],"Add 12 hours for afternoon.")
H('474.d.2.D',4,"A patient is given a medicine at 2100 and the next dose is due 8 hours later. The next dose time in military time is:","0500",["2900","0900","0700"],"2100 + 8 hours = 0500 next day.")
H('474.d.2.E',3,"A nurse estimates that 48 pills split among 5 bottles is about 10 per bottle. She is using:","estimation",["exact counting","guessing wildly","measuring"],"Estimation checks reasonableness.")
H('474.d.2.E',4,"Rounding 19.8 mL to the nearest whole number for a quick check gives:","20 mL",["19 mL","18 mL","21 mL"],"Round to nearest whole.")
H('474.d.2.F',3,"The Roman numeral IV in a health record stands for:","4",["6","9","14"],"IV = 4.")
H('474.d.2.F',4,"The Roman numeral XIV equals:","14",["16","24","15"],"X + IV = 14.")
H('474.d.3.A',3,"A scatterplot of hours exercised and resting heart rate lets a student see whether the two variables are:","related",["blue","identical","random labels"],"Scatterplots show relationships.")
H('474.d.3.A',4,"Fitting a line to a scatterplot of dose and response is using a function to model the:","trend in the data",["calendar","rainfall","school"],"Models fit data.")
H('474.d.3.B',3,"A medicine's amount in the blood after each hour is half the amount from the hour before. This pattern is modeled by an:","exponential function",["linear function","constant","absolute value"],"Halving repeatedly is exponential decay.")
H('474.d.3.B',4,"A function with a constant rate of change, such as an IV that drips 30 mL each hour, is called:","linear",["exponential","periodic","logarithmic"],"Constant change is linear.")
H('474.d.3.C',3,"A patient's breathing rises and falls in a repeating pattern. Repeating patterns like this are modeled using a:","sinusoidal function",["constant","linear equation","absolute value"],"Waves are sinusoidal.")
H('474.d.3.C',4,"The time it takes for one full breathing cycle on a sinusoidal graph is called the:","period",["slope","intercept","range"],"Period is the length of one cycle.")
H('474.d.3.D',3,"Two medicines are mixed to form a solution of a desired strength. Finding the amounts of each uses a system of:","equations",["recipes","posters","charts only"],"Mixtures lead to systems.")
H('474.d.3.D',4,"If x + y = 10 and x - y = 4, then x is:","7",["3","6","14"],"Adding gives 2x = 14, so x = 7.")
H('474.d.3.E',3,"The growth of bacteria in a lab dish that doubles every hour can be solved using properties of:","exponential functions",["linear functions","right triangles","proportions only"],"Doubling is exponential.")
H('474.d.3.E',4,"The inverse of an exponential function, used to solve for time in a growth problem, is the:","logarithm",["square root","absolute value","reciprocal"],"Logs undo exponentials.")
H('474.d.3.F',3,"A unit rate compares a quantity to one unit. If an IV delivers 120 mL in 4 hours, the unit rate is:","30 mL per hour",["4 mL per hour","480 mL per hour","120 hours per mL"],"120 / 4 = 30.")
H('474.d.3.F',4,"A pharmacy fills 90 prescriptions in 5 hours. The unit rate is:","18 prescriptions per hour",["450 per hour","5 per hour","85 per hour"],"90 / 5 = 18.")
H('474.d.4.A',3,"A dietitian, a nurse, and a radiologic technologist each use math in different ways. Each profession requires a unique set of:","skills",["colors","songs","games"],"Professions differ in math use.")
H('474.d.4.A',4,"Dental hygienists measure pocket depths in millimeters, while pharmacists calculate doses in milligrams. Both use math, but with different:","units and tools",["names only","holidays","seasons"],"Fields use different units.")
H('474.d.4.B',3,"Measuring a patient's height wrongly could change a medicine dose based on body size, so accurate measurements are necessary to protect:","patient safety",["staff breaks","parking","menus"],"Accuracy prevents harm.")
H('474.d.4.B',4,"A pharmacy scale off by 5 percent could give patients too much or too little of a drug. This shows why measurements must be:","accurate",["fast","colorful","loud"],"Accuracy matters.")
H('474.d.4.C',3,"To change 2.5 kg to grams, a technician multiplies by 1,000 using the method of dimensional analysis, which keeps track of the:","units",["colors","names","dates"],"Units cancel in dimensional analysis.")
H('474.d.4.C',4,"Using dimensional analysis, an IV running at 30 mL per minute, multiplied by 60 minutes per hour, delivers:","1,800 mL per hour",["90 mL per hour","0.5 mL per hour","180 mL per hour"],"30 x 60 = 1,800 and the minutes cancel.")
H('474.d.4.D',3,"Teaspoons and tablespoons belong to the household system, while milliliters belong to the:","metric system",["Roman system","apothecary system","nautical system"],"Classify units by system.")
H('474.d.4.D',4,"Grains and drams are old units that belong to the:","apothecary system",["metric system","SI system","decimal system"],"Apothecary units are old.")
H('474.d.4.E',3,"To measure the temperature of a patient, a nurse selects a thermometer. To measure weight, she selects a:","scale",["ruler","stopwatch","protractor"],"Right tool for the quantity.")
H('474.d.4.E',4,"A goniometer measures the angle of a joint. Choosing it for this job is selecting an appropriate:","measurement tool",["recipe","diagnosis","bill"],"Tools match tasks.")
H('474.d.4.F',3,"A nurse takes a pulse by counting beats for 15 seconds and multiplying by 4. She is using a measurement:","technique",["accident","color","rumor"],"Techniques give measurements.")
H('474.d.4.F',4,"To find an accurate blood pressure, a nurse places the cuff at heart level and rests the patient first, using proper measurement:","procedures",["rumors","tricks","guesses"],"Proper technique improves accuracy.")
H('474.d.5.A',3,"A lab report shows a patient's blood sugar is above the normal range. A health worker compares the value to the reference range to see if it lies:","outside normal limits",["inside the lab","on the report","near the front"],"Reference ranges guide interpretation.")
H('474.d.5.A',4,"A hemoglobin result below the reference range is flagged because it may indicate:","a health problem",["a normal result","a printing error only","good health"],"Values outside limits need attention.")
H('474.d.5.B',3,"A resting adult heart rate of 140 beats per minute is above the typical range of about 60 to 100. A nurse comparing this to normal parameters would note it as:","abnormally high",["normal","slightly low","perfect"],"Vital signs have ranges.")
H('474.d.5.B',4,"A temperature of 98.6 degrees Fahrenheit is considered:","normal body temperature",["a fever","hypothermia","shock"],"98.6 is the usual average.")
H('474.d.5.C',3,"The average of 70, 72, and 74 beats per minute is:","72",["70","74","216"],"(70 + 72 + 74)/3 = 72.")
H('474.d.5.C',4,"The median of the blood glucose values 90, 100, 95, 120, and 105 is:","100",["95","105","102"],"Ordered 90, 95, 100, 105, 120: middle is 100.")
H('474.d.5.D',3,"Many biological measurements such as height follow a bell-shaped curve called the:","normal distribution",["straight line","square wave","spiral"],"Normal curves are symmetric.")
H('474.d.5.D',4,"In a normal distribution, the mean, median, and mode are all located at the:","center",["far left","far right","bottom"],"They coincide at the peak.")
H('474.d.5.E',3,"According to the Empirical Rule, about 68 percent of data in a normal distribution fall within how many standard deviations of the mean?","one",["two","three","four"],"68-95-99.7.")
H('474.d.5.E',4,"If the mean cholesterol is 190 with a standard deviation of 20, about 95 percent of values fall between:","150 and 230",["170 and 210","130 and 250","190 and 210"],"190 plus or minus 40.")
H('474.d.5.F',3,"A z-score tells how many standard deviations a value is from the mean. A value equal to the mean has a z-score of:","0",["1","-1","100"],"The mean is zero deviations away.")
H('474.d.5.F',4,"A patient's score is 80 when the mean is 70 and the standard deviation is 5. The z-score is:","2",["10","5","0.5"],"(80 - 70)/5 = 2.")
H('474.d.5.G',3,"A child's height is at the 75th percentile. This means the child is taller than about 75 percent of children of the same:","age",["name","state","weight only"],"Percentiles compare to a group.")
H('474.d.5.G',4,"If 18 of 20 students scored lower than a student, her percentile rank is:","90",["18","20","10"],"18/20 = 90 percent.")
H('474.d.5.H',3,"A well-designed clinical experiment uses a control group, random assignment, and a large enough:","sample",["budget only","logo","slogan"],"Good design reduces bias.")
H('474.d.5.H',4,"Assigning patients to treatment and control groups by chance is called:","randomization",["favoritism","guessing","sorting by age"],"Random assignment reduces bias.")
H('474.d.5.I',3,"A study surveys 200 patients to learn about all patients in a hospital. The 200 patients are a:","sample",["population","census","parameter"],"A sample is a part of the group.")
H('474.d.5.I',4,"All of the patients in a hospital make up the:","population",["sample","control","bias"],"The population is the whole group.")
H('474.d.5.J',3,"In a drug trial, a pill with no active ingredient is a placebo, and the improvement some patients report from it is the placebo:","effect",["error","price","dose"],"Expectation can affect results.")
H('474.d.5.J',4,"Researchers use a placebo group so that they can tell whether a drug works better than:","a pill with no active ingredient",["no patients","a larger dose","the first trial"],"Control is needed.")
H('474.d.5.K',3,"The study of how often diseases occur in groups of people and what affects them is called:","epidemiology",["anatomy","chemistry","physiology"],"Epidemiology uses statistics.")
H('474.d.5.K',4,"An epidemiologist who counts new flu cases each week and compares them across counties is using statistics to help guide:","public health decisions",["sports schedules","fashion trends","tax laws"],"Statistics support public health.")
H('474.d.6.A',3,"The volume of a rectangular tank 20 cm by 10 cm by 5 cm is:","1,000 cubic centimeters",["35 cubic centimeters","200 cubic centimeters","100 cubic centimeters"],"20 x 10 x 5 = 1,000.")
H('474.d.6.A',4,"A cylinder-shaped medicine bottle has a radius of 2 cm and a height of 10 cm. Using pi = 3.14, its volume is about:","125.6 cubic centimeters",["62.8 cubic centimeters","40 cubic centimeters","31.4 cubic centimeters"],"3.14 x 4 x 10 = 125.6.")
H('474.d.6.B',3,"A burn covers a rectangle of skin 10 cm by 6 cm. Its surface area is:","60 square centimeters",["16 square centimeters","32 square centimeters","600 square centimeters"],"10 x 6 = 60.")
H('474.d.6.B',4,"The surface area of a circular bandage with a radius of 3 cm is about, using pi = 3.14:","28.3 square centimeters",["9.4 square centimeters","18.8 square centimeters","56.5 square centimeters"],"3.14 x 9 = 28.26.")
H('474.d.6.C',3,"A therapist positions a patient's arm so that it forms a right angle. The angle measures:","90 degrees",["45 degrees","180 degrees","360 degrees"],"Right angle is 90.")
H('474.d.6.C',4,"Two angles in a straight line, one of 135 degrees, require a second angle of:","45 degrees",["135 degrees","90 degrees","225 degrees"],"Supplementary angles add to 180.")
H('474.d.6.D',3,"A goniometer reads a knee bending from 10 to 130 degrees. The range of motion is:","120 degrees",["60 degrees","140 degrees","240 degrees"],"Range = end minus start.")
H('474.d.6.D',4,"A patient's elbow begins at 20 degrees and bends to 135 degrees. The range of motion is:","115 degrees",["135 degrees","155 degrees","20 degrees"],"135 - 20 = 115.")

